Description: Manage a window that asks to be mapped as an ordinary window
 The window manager took a window's override-redirect flag from its
 CreateNotify and kept it. Wine creates a fullscreen window
 override-redirect and clears the flag before it maps the window, so the
 window manager framed and showed the window but, counting it
 override-redirect, never gave it the input focus, answered none of its
 ConfigureRequests and sent it no ConfigureNotify; the X focus stayed None
 and the program's keys reached no window. A MapRequest comes only for a
 window that is not override-redirect, so the window manager now clears the
 flag there.
Author: Rach2
Forwarded: no
---
--- a/xwayland/window-manager.c
+++ b/xwayland/window-manager.c
@@ -1297,6 +1297,11 @@
 	if (!wm_lookup_window(wm, map_request->window, &window))
 		return;
 
+	/* The X server redirects the map of a window only when it is not
+	 * override-redirect, so a client that created the window as one has
+	 * since made it an ordinary window, as Wine does; manage it as one. */
+	window->override_redirect = 0;
+
 	weston_wm_window_read_properties(window);
 
 	/* For a new Window, MapRequest happens before the Window is realized
